DETAILS for CCS:
carbon positive CCS; Most carbon leaves the refinery as fuel products and is later released when burned, so total emissions exceed the CO₂ captured on site

near carbon CCS; use coal to produce the electricity, and the electricity is the energy which does not cause the emission of the carbon. During producing 90% of the carbon will be captured by CCS, and its production does not emit additional co2 to the atomsphere.

carbon negative CCS; 
1. the co2 is captured by the plants into the biomass.
2. a fraction of carbon turn to ethanol, finally back to atomsphere via burnning
3.The remaining carbon is captured during conversion and geologically stored – this portion makes the overall balance negative.

biomass: wood is one of the biomass, it is the source that stores the energy from the sun and via plant's photosynthesis.

